# Every environment file, not just the ones we happened to think of.
#
# `.env`, `.env.local` and `.env.*.local` were listed by name, so a `.env.prod`
# — the file that would hold live database URLs and payment keys — was tracked.
# This repository is public: a secret committed here is a secret published.
#
# A named list of secret files always ends up missing one, and it is always the
# one someone just invented.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.DS_Store
coverage/

